{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012iwhWjBQf9tcugAK2NiYHV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd053-sort\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/sort: Sort Lines of Text Files\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Sort is a foundational text processing utility used in virtually every Unix pipeline\n6\t  that requires ordered data. The macOS BSD sort differs from GNU sort in collation\n7\t  behavior, numeric parsing, and key field syntax. The Go implementation must match the\n8\t  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gsort, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all\n9\t  flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils. All tests use\n10\t  LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n11\t\n12\tgoals:\n13\t  - G1: Sort input lines lexicographically by default, with configurable key fields and ordering.\n14\t  - G2: Support numeric, human-numeric, month, version, and random sort modes.\n15\t  - G3: Support field-based sorting with key specifications (-k) and field separators (-t).\n16\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gsort via differential testing.\n17\t\n18\trequirements:\n19\t  R1:\n20\t    title: Basic sorting and output control\n21\t    items:\n22\t      - R1.1:\n23\t          text: When no flags are given, must sort all input lines lexicographically using byte values (LC_ALL=C).\n24\t      - R1.2:\n25\t          text: Must read from stdin when no file arguments are given or when a file argument is \"-\".\n26\t      - R1.3:\n27\t          text: Must accept multiple input files and sort their combined lines as a single stream.\n28\t      - R1.4:\n29\t          text: \"-r or --reverse must reverse the sort order.\"\n30\t      - R1.5:\n31\t          text: \"-u or --unique must output only the first of an equal run (based on the active sort key).\"\n32\t      - R1.6:\n33\t          text: \"-o FILE or --output=FILE must write output to FILE. FILE may be the same as an input file.\"\n34\t      - R1.7:\n35\t          text: \"-s or --stable must preserve the input order of lines that compare equal.\"\n36\t\n37\t  R2:\n38\t    title: Sort modes\n39\t    items:\n40\t      - R2.1:\n41\t          text: \"-n or --numeric-sort must sort by numeric value, parsing leading whitespace and optional sign.\"\n42\t      - R2.2:\n43\t          text: \"-h or --human-numeric-sort must sort by numeric value with SI suffixes (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y).\"\n44\t      - R2.3:\n45\t          text: \"-M or --month-sort must sort by month name abbreviation (JAN < FEB < ... < DEC). Unknown strings sort before JAN.\"\n46\t      - R2.4:\n47\t          text: \"-V or --version-sort must sort by version number segments (natural sort).\"\n48\t\n49\t  R3:\n50\t    title: Key fields and delimiters\n51\t    items:\n52\t      - R3.1:\n53\t          text: \"-t CHAR or --field-separator=CHAR must use CHAR as the field delimiter instead of the default blank-to-non-blank transition.\"\n54\t      - R3.2:\n55\t          text: \"-k KEYDEF or --key=KEYDEF must sort by the specified key field. KEYDEF format is F[.C][OPTS][,F[.C][OPTS]] where F is field number, C is character position, and OPTS are modifier letters (n, r, h, M, V, b, d, f, i).\"\n56\t      - R3.3:\n57\t          text: Must support multiple -k options. Earlier keys take precedence; later keys break ties.\n58\t      - R3.4:\n59\t          text: \"-b or --ignore-leading-blanks must ignore leading blanks when finding sort keys.\"\n60\t\n61\t  R4:\n62\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n63\t    items:\n64\t      - R4.1:\n65\t          text: Must exit 0 when input is sorted successfully.\n66\t      - R4.2:\n67\t          text: \"-c or --check must check whether input is sorted. Exit 0 if sorted, exit 1 if not. With -C or --check=quiet, suppress the diagnostic message.\"\n68\t      - R4.3:\n69\t          text: Must exit 2 on usage errors (invalid flags, conflicting options).\n70\t      - R4.4:\n71\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: default sort, -r, -n, -h, -M, -V, -u, -s, -k with field specs, -t delimiter, -b, -c check mode, multi-file input, and stdin.\"\n72\t\n73\tnon_goals:\n74\t  - cmd/sort does not implement --parallel (threaded merge sort). Single-threaded sorting is sufficient for correctness verification.\n75\t  - cmd/sort does not implement --compress-program for external merge with compression.\n76\t  - cmd/sort does not implement -R (random sort with hash). Random output cannot be verified by differential testing.\n77\t  - cmd/sort does not implement --files0-from for reading file lists from NUL-delimited input.\n78\t  - cmd/sort does not implement external merge sort for inputs larger than available memory.\n79\t\n80\tacceptance_criteria:\n81\t  - id: AC1\n82\t    criterion: \"printf 'banana\\\\napple\\\\ncherry\\\\n' | go run ./cmd/sort produces apple, banana, cherry, matching gsort.\"\n83\t    traces:\n84\t      - R1.1\n85\t      - R1.2\n86\t      - R1.3\n87\t      - R1.4\n88\t      - R1.5\n89\t      - R1.6\n90\t      - R1.7\n91\t  - id: AC2\n92\t    criterion: \"printf '10\\\\n2\\\\n1\\\\n' | go run ./cmd/sort -n produces 1, 2, 10, matching gsort.\"\n93\t    traces:\n94\t      - R2.1\n95\t      - R4.4\n96\t  - id: AC3\n97\t    criterion: \"sort -k2,2 -t: on colon-delimited input produces correct field-based ordering, matching gsort.\"\n98\t    traces:\n99\t      - R3.1\n100\t      - R4.4\n101\t  - id: AC4\n102\t    criterion: \"sort -c on unsorted input exits 1, matching gsort.\"\n103\t    traces:\n104\t      - R4.1\n105\t      - R4.2\n106\t      - R4.3\n107\t      - R4.4\n108\t  - id: AC5\n109\t    criterion: \"sort -u removes duplicate lines based on the active key, matching gsort.\"\n110\t    traces:\n111\t      - R1.5\n112\t      - R4.4\n113\t  - id: AC6\n114\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gsort passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n115\t    traces:\n116\t      - R4.4\n117\t  - id: AC7\n118\t    criterion: \"cmd/sort compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n119\t    traces:\n120\t      - R1.1\n121\t      - R1.2\n122\t      - R1.3\n123\t      - R1.4\n124\t      - R1.5\n125\t      - R1.6\n126\t      - R1.7\n127\t      - R2.1\n128\t      - R2.2\n129\t      - R2.3\n130\t      - R2.4\n131\t      - R3.1\n132\t      - R3.2\n133\t      - R3.3\n134\t      - R3.4\n135\t      - R4.1\n136\t      - R4.2\n137\t      - R4.3\n138\t      - R4.4\n139\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fed53ede-a912-463f-bf3c-6e3e60d7c2c3","uuid":"4f13f914-a042-4e9a-b929-f870e9eddeb7","timestamp":"2026-05-20T14:58:44.119Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5374/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd053-sort.yaml","content":"id: srd053-sort\ntitle: \"cmd/sort: Sort Lines of Text Files\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Sort is a foundational text processing utility used in virtually every Unix pipeline\n  that requires ordered data. The macOS BSD sort differs from GNU sort in collation\n  behavior, numeric parsing, and key field syntax. The Go implementation must match the\n  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gsort, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all\n  flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils. All tests use\n  LC_ALL=C to eliminate locale-dependent divergence.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Sort input lines lexicographically by default, with configurable key fields and ordering.\n  - G2: Support numeric, human-numeric, month, version, and random sort modes.\n  - G3: Support field-based sorting with key specifications (-k) and field separators (-t).\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gsort via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Basic sorting and output control\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: When no flags are given, must sort all input lines lexicographically using byte values (LC_ALL=C).\n      - R1.2:\n          text: Must read from stdin when no file arguments are given or when a file argument is \"-\".\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must accept multiple input files and sort their combined lines as a single stream.\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"-r or --reverse must reverse the sort order.\"\n      - R1.5:\n          text: \"-u or --unique must output only the first of an equal run (based on the active sort key).\"\n      - R1.6:\n          text: \"-o FILE or --output=FILE must write output to FILE. FILE may be the same as an input file.\"\n      - R1.7:\n          text: \"-s or --stable must preserve the input order of lines that compare equal.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Sort modes\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-n or --numeric-sort must sort by numeric value, parsing leading whitespace and optional sign.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-h or --human-numeric-sort must sort by numeric value with SI suffixes (K, M, G, T, P, E, Z, Y).\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-M or --month-sort must sort by month name abbreviation (JAN < FEB < ... < DEC). Unknown strings sort before JAN.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"-V or --version-sort must sort by version number segments (natural sort).\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Key fields and delimiters\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-t CHAR or --field-separator=CHAR must use CHAR as the field delimiter instead of the default blank-to-non-blank transition.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"-k KEYDEF or --key=KEYDEF must sort by the specified key field. KEYDEF format is F[.C][OPTS][,F[.C][OPTS]] where F is field number, C is character position, and OPTS are modifier letters (n, r, h, M, V, b, d, f, i).\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must support multiple -k options. Earlier keys take precedence; later keys break ties.\n      - R3.4:\n          text: \"-b or --ignore-leading-blanks must ignore leading blanks when finding sort keys.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when input is sorted successfully.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"-c or --check must check whether input is sorted. Exit 0 if sorted, exit 1 if not. With -C or --check=quiet, suppress the diagnostic message.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: Must exit 2 on usage errors (invalid flags, conflicting options).\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Differential tests must compare stdout output and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: default sort, -r, -n, -h, -M, -V, -u, -s, -k with field specs, -t delimiter, -b, -c check mode, multi-file input, and stdin.\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/sort does not implement --parallel (threaded merge sort). Single-threaded sorting is sufficient for correctness verification.\n  - cmd/sort does not implement --compress-program for external merge with compression.\n  - cmd/sort does not implement -R (random sort with hash). Random output cannot be verified by differential testing.\n  - cmd/sort does not implement --files0-from for reading file lists from NUL-delimited input.\n  - cmd/sort does not implement external merge sort for inputs larger than available memory.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"printf 'banana\\\\napple\\\\ncherry\\\\n' | go run ./cmd/sort produces apple, banana, cherry, matching gsort.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R1.7\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"printf '10\\\\n2\\\\n1\\\\n' | go run ./cmd/sort -n produces 1, 2, 10, matching gsort.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"sort -k2,2 -t: on colon-delimited input produces correct field-based ordering, matching gsort.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"sort -c on unsorted input exits 1, matching gsort.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"sort -u removes duplicate lines based on the active key, matching gsort.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.5\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gsort passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC7\n    criterion: \"cmd/sort compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R1.5\n      - R1.6\n      - R1.7\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":139,"startLine":1,"totalLines":139}}}
